FAULT 1 — Foxglove bridge had no route to the Gazebo server. FIXED.
  Evidence before:
    bridge nets: ao-html-window=10.89.14.37
    server nets: ao-sim-fabrication=10.89.5.24
    /proc/net/route inside bridge: only 000E590A/00FFFFFF (10.89.14.0/24)
    connect 10.89.5.24:11345 -> "Network is unreachable"
  Cause: quadlet declared only Network=ao-html-window.network. gz-transport
  discovery is UDP multicast on the local link, so both containers must share
  one L2 segment. A matching GZ_PARTITION does not route between two separate
  Internal=true bridges.
  Fix: added second Network=ao-sim-fabrication.network to the bridge quadlet.
  Correction recorded in-file: the old header note claimed "reachability comes
  from the loopback publish, not from network egress" citing ao-mapping ->
  ao-webodm-web on 8000. That is a category error — the loopback publish makes
  the VIEWER reach the BRIDGE; it does nothing for the BRIDGE reaching the
  SERVER, which travels over gz-transport. The cited precedent never bridged
  across networks and was never like-for-like.

FAULT 2 — Gazebo camera sensor never instantiated. FIXED.
  Evidence before: the running server logged ZERO "CameraSensor" lines and never
  advertised /factory/camera/image. Only the 20:37 run on 2026-10-01 had loaded
  the Sensors system, and uniquely it did NOT print
  "No systems loaded from SDF, loading defaults".
  Cause: $GZHOME/.gz/sim/10/server.config names only 3 systems (Physics,
  UserCommands, SceneBroadcaster). Without a world-level <plugin> block Gazebo
  loads exactly those 3. No Sensors system means no render thread, so the camera
  sensor is never created — SILENTLY. The server looks completely healthy.
  A/B PROVEN in throwaway containers, same image, same world apart from the block:
    control (no plugin block) -> 0 x "CameraSensor", topic absent
    fix    (plugin block)    -> Sensors system loaded; ogre2 headless;
                                "Camera images ... advertised on
                                 [/factory/camera/image]"
  Fix: added an explicit world-level <plugin> block to
  GAZEBO/worlds/factory.world (Sensors first, then UserCommands,
  SceneBroadcaster, Physics).
  Verified live: server restarted 2026-10-02 12:12:08 and logged
  "Camera images for [camera_rig::camera_rig::user_camera] advertised on
  [/factory/camera/image]".

FAULT 3 — the bridge container could not load its own libraries. FIXED.
  This was the real reason the viewer was empty, and it was SILENT.
  Evidence:
    ldconfig -p | grep -c gz            -> 0
    find / -name 'libgz-*'              -> only under /opt/ros/lyrical/opt/
    missing: /opt/ros/lyrical/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu  (libfastcdr.so.2,
             librmw_fastrtps_cpp.so — the ROS middleware itself)
    missing: the five gz_*_vendor/lib dirs (libgz-transport.so.15,
             libgz-msgs.so.12)
  The previous LD_LIBRARY_PATH listed only three directories. Symptoms on top of
  the silence: "dlopen error: libfastcdr.so.2: cannot open shared object file"
  and "failed to load any RMW implementations".
  Fix: entrypoint now exports /opt/ros/lyrical/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu plus all
  five gz_*_vendor/lib directories.

FAULT 4 — wrong bridge executable and wrong type mapping. FIXED.
  Evidence:
    bridge_node with the previous -p topic:=/factory/camera/image@ros2 and
    -p bridge_type:=gz.msgs.Image  -> stays alive, logs NOTHING, creates NO
    publisher (confirmed with `ros2 node info /ros_gz_bridge`: Publishers
    listed only /parameter_events and /rosout). Bridged nothing, silently.
    Naming the gz type alone ->
      "No template specialization for the pair"
    Correct spec, which logs and works:
      parameter_bridge '/factory/camera/image@sensor_msgs/msg/Image[gz.msgs.Image'
      -> "Creating GZ->ROS Bridge: [/factory/camera/image (gz.msgs.Image)
                                 -> /factory/camera/image (sensor_msgs/msg/Image)]"
  '[' is the direction bracket for Gazebo -> ROS ONLY, which is what this
  view-only surface requires. Verified view-only: the live bridge logs exactly
  one "Creating GZ->ROS Bridge" line and NO "Creating ROS->GZ" line, and no
  /world/*/control topic is bridged.
  Fix: GZ_BRIDGE now points at parameter_bridge, not bridge_node.

